  <!-- Abstract Lead -->
  <p class="lead">
    Measurements of the cosmological matter dipole inferred from distant active galactic nuclei (AGN) have persistently reported amplitudes twice as large as the kinematic dipole benchmark predicted by standard &Lambda;CDM cosmology. In this work, we conduct an end-to-end systematics audit and establish the first joint hierarchical Bayesian Poisson co-inference framework evaluating <strong>2,865,080 all-sky cosmic sources</strong> simultaneously across three independent wavelength domains: optical (<em>Gaia</em> DR3 &times; <em>unWISE</em> Quaia: 1,295,502 quasars), mid-infrared (CatWISE2020: 1,360,788 AGNs), and radio (NVSS: 208,790 sources).
  </p>

  <!-- Interactive Model Embed -->
